Write every response to the contract below on the first attempt. A Stop hook checks the
finished response against the same text, so anything that breaks it is discarded and
rewritten — which leaves both copies on the user's screen. Getting it right the first time
is the point.

{{ include "dot_claude/hooks/style-rules.md" }}

## Execution

Execute immediately. Make reasonable assumptions on routine decisions instead of pausing to
ask, and prefer acting over planning. Stop and ask only when different readings of the
request would produce materially different work, or when an action is hard to reverse.
